title: The Last Thesis
subtitle: The debate turns on the clause about expulsions.
view-if: congress = 1 and congress_heidelberg = 1 and congress_closing = 0 and heid_cg_thesis = 0 and heid_motion <= 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.heid_cg_thesis = 1;
var sp = RG.speaker('luxemburgist');
Q.heid_speaker_name = sp.name;
Q.heid_speaker_power = sp.power;
RG.congress.tally();
!}
frequency: 400
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: congress

= The Last Thesis

On the second day the debate stops being about elections and becomes about the party itself. [? if heid_motion = 1 : Wolffheim calls the last thesis a guillotine with a footnote. ?][? if heid_motion = 2 : The Left Radicals say the missing thesis is still there, in invisible ink. ?] The Saxon delegates ask whether a young party can afford to throw out half of itself. [+ heid_speaker_name +] will answer for the Zentrale tonight.

- @firm: A party is a discipline, or it is nothing.
- @drop: Drop the clause, and win the waverers.
- @restore: Put the clause back, and name the districts it means.
- @natbol: Read out the Hamburg articles on a people's war.

@firm
subtitle: Our best speaker against theirs.
on-arrival: {!
RG.congress.sway(0.04 * Q.heid_speaker_power);
RG.congress.bitter(2);
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

[+ heid_speaker_name +] speaks for an hour and a half without a note. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates are won over before the end. ?][? if congress_last_moved = 0 : The hall applauds, and nobody changes sides. ?] Our side has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall.

@drop
view-if: heid_motion = 1
subtitle: The Left Radicals stay. The Zentrale's own people will feel betrayed.
on-arrival: {!
Q.heid_motion = 2;
RG.congress.sway(0.07);
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 6;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The Zentrale withdraws the last thesis in the middle of the debate. Our side has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall. Some of our own delegates are not speaking to the Zentrale.

@restore
view-if: heid_motion = 2
subtitle: The Spartacists will be glad. The waverers will not.
on-arrival: {!
Q.heid_motion = 1;
RG.congress.lose(0.05);
RG.congress.bitter(4);
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
!}

Our side has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall, and the Left Radicals know exactly where they stand.

@natbol
view-if: heid_natbol = 1
subtitle: Bremen dislikes Laufenberg's nationalism. It may break with Hamburg tonight.
on-arrival: {!
var n = RG.congress.convert('bremen', 0.35) + RG.congress.convert('berlin', 0.1);
RG.congress.tally();
Q.congress_last_moved = n;
RG.congress.bitter(3);
!}

The articles are read aloud, slowly, with the officers' letters of thanks after them. The Bremen delegates go out to confer. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates come back to vote with us. ?] Our side has [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the hall.
